+"""Video counting, v2: configurable counting rules on top of the v1 pipeline.
+
+Changes with respect to count_in_videos_pseudo_exemplars.py:
+
+1. stage 3 (seed + branch A + count) is delegated to ``counting_rules.track_and_count``
+   so the same code can be unit-tested and replayed offline;
+2. the new-object rule can be ``strict`` (v1, zero overlap) or ``coverage``
+   (uncovered-area fraction), see --rule/--min_uncovered;
+3. duplicate tracks can be merged after propagation (--merge_tracks/--handover);
+4. pseudo-exemplars can be selected for spatial diversity instead of top-k score
+   only (--exemplar_strategy diverse);
+5. branch A no longer repeats the first batch of boxes when a frame adds more
+   than --obj_batch_size objects (v1 bug);
+6. stage-1/2 outputs can be cached (--save_cache) and stage 3 alone can be
+   re-run from a cache (--replay_cache), which makes rule sweeps take minutes;
+7. mask IoU uses a vectorised implementation (same values, ~20x faster on the
+   temporal filter).
+
+Defaults reproduce v1 behaviour exactly, apart from the branch-A bug fix.
+"""
